  "authoritative_metadata": "manifest.json",
  "title": "Reading the atoms through glue",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "Reading the atoms through glue. The two-stage twin rule (twins first pick out the atom lines, the lines in twin classes of two or more; then twins compared on atom lines alone give the atoms) is CHAIN-TRANSFER C's rule on every Fano tree, so it reads the atoms of every Fano tree whose atoms have at most four cuts (proved). Computed with exact creation maps: it reads the atoms of every one of BRACE-TREE C's 111 fresh spaces and of most random spaces with plane glue, adding to an atom only doubled-square lines; where it fails it merges atoms that meet one planar brace or drops a line of an atom. In most failing spaces, two lines of different atoms create at each other and at, and from, exactly the same lines: exchanging them is a symmetry of the yes/no creation relation, so no rule that reads only whether creation occurs can return the atoms there. Which far side creates separates every two lines of different atoms in all 191 spaces, but it varies inside atoms too, so twins far side by far side do not read the atoms even on Fano trees; reading every three-fold space needs a rule that uses which far side creates.",
